{"title":"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Trig_Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Trig Bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(No_Trig)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (No Trig)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Intuitive_and_Quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Intuitive and Quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Very_Bashy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Very Bashy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(easy_to_digest)_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (easy to digest) by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(⚡Solved_in_56_seconds⚡)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (⚡Solved in 56 seconds⚡)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Usain is walking for exercise by zigzagging across a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />-meter by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-meter rectangular field, beginning at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and ending on the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. He wants to increase the distance walked by zigzagging as shown in the figure below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/9/1a91fc20f2dad7aee91e927cd48f3773414ff22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(APQRS)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" />. What angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/582debb94a73d226fa0d4ae31f6e427ada7ee4c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\angle PAB=\\angle QPC=\\angle RQB=\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"299\" height=\"18\" /> will produce a length that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> meters? (This figure is not drawn to scale. Do not assume that he zigzag path has exactly four segments as shown; there could be more or fewer.)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/f/32f79492cfd57de5bd7b5008d86027a497703c9a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; draw((-50,15)--(50,15)); draw((50,15)--(50,-15)); draw((50,-15)--(-50,-15)); draw((-50,-15)--(-50,15)); draw((-50,-15)--(-22.5,15)); draw((-22.5,15)--(5,-15)); draw((5,-15)--(32.5,15)); draw((32.5,15)--(50,-4.090909090909)); label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;, (-41.5,-10.5)); label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;, (-13,10.5)); label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;, (15.5,-10.5)); label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;, (43,10.5)); dot((-50,15)); dot((-50,-15)); dot((50,15)); dot((50,-15)); dot((50,-4.09090909090909)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(-58,15)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(-58,-15)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(58,15)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(58,-15)); label(&quot;$S$&quot;,(58,-4.0909090909)); dot((-22.5,15)); dot((5,-15)); dot((32.5,15)); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,(-22.5,23)); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;,(5,-23)); label(&quot;$R$&quot;,(32.5,23)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"112\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a9864b4e1cc737d947ddec30248092f769af248.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~\\arccos\\frac{5}{6}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}~\\arccos\\frac{4}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}~\\arccos\\frac{3}{10}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}~\\arcsin\\frac{4}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}~\\arcsin\\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"650\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By \"unfolding\" <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/541e91caa3cea152c639902a2d6b52cd0cb8054c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> into a straight line, we get a right angled triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/1/8d1510c876b425003ac68b381baf26be70a723e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABS&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/54838167dbf7d6021453ab5b6a6420e393a15a72.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; draw((-50,15)--(50,15)); draw((50,15)--(50,-15)); draw((50,-15)--(-50,-15)); draw((-50,-15)--(-50,15)); draw((-50,-15)--(-22.5,15)); draw((-22.5,15)--(5,-15)); draw((5,-15)--(32.5,15)); draw((32.5,15)--(50,-4.090909090909)); label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;, (-41.5,-10.5)); label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;, (-13,10.5)); label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;, (15.5,-10.5)); label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;, (43,10.5)); dot((-50,15)); dot((-50,-15)); dot((50,15)); dot((50,-15)); dot((50,-4.09090909090909)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(-58,15)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(-58,-15)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(58,15)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(58,-15)); label(&quot;$S$&quot;,(58,-4.0909090909)); dot((-22.5,15)); dot((5,-15)); dot((32.5,15)); dot((5,45)); dot((32.5,75)); dot((50,94.09090909090909)); draw((-22.5,15)--(50,94.09090909090909)); draw((50,-4.09090909090909)--(50,94.09090909090909)); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,(-22.5,23)); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;,(5,-23)); label(&quot;$R$&quot;,(32.5,23)); label(&quot;$Q&#39;$&quot;,(5,35)); label(&quot;$R&#39;$&quot;,(32.5,85)); label(&quot;$S&#39;$&quot;,(58,94.09090909090909)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\nIt follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69f6ffda4eff26b5ebb76f5fc601809faf838dde.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\cos(\\theta)&amp;=\\frac{100}{120} \\\\ \\theta&amp;=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } \\arccos\\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"215\" height=\"97\" />\n~lptoggled\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Drop an altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and let its base be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Note that if we repeat this for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, all four right triangles (including <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de532b06931879197f8d75bc6385efa273985f0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{RSC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />) will have the same trig ratios. By proportion, the hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23f7d960825f3e1f2aa58d08df4ee15c28c2d22b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{100}(120) = \\frac65 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"122\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/1833cce4fab39687cf08fa84a9d15fe23510676e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta = \\frac{x}{(\\frac65x)} = \\frac56 \\Rightarrow \\theta = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\arccos{\\frac56}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"315\" height=\"50\" />.\n</p><p>~IbrahimNadeem\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Trig_Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Trig_Bash)\">Solution 3 (Trig Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Trig Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the length of one of the full segments of the zigzag. We can then notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/e/08edbda629f7813ae3812cf00708d1c0790a8b30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta = \\frac{30}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"38\" />. By Pythagorean Theorem, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/4/4c4bf9b80d2a3de8c5b580af085b553a9b51922e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DP = \\sqrt{x^2 - 900}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"138\" height=\"21\" />. This implies that: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e25bf29893cac02f79d5cd23c044166e48ae6f4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[RC = 100 - 3\\sqrt{x^2 - 900}.\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" /> We also realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/c/d1c89971392a7a61f382c9427840d9e69fd49598.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS = 120 - 3x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"16\" />, so this means that: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/b/42bd032254cf7f1c2aaa139559c5cf8de89caa37.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos\\theta = \\frac{100 - 3\\sqrt{x^2 - 900}}{120 - 3x}.\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"40\" /> We can then substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/4/384b94c6ff77c002670cc255e436c8f46ed1737c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{30}{\\sin\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"38\" />, so this gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/552d620401949fb211e5dcc88dfabffb4d139a85.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\cos\\theta &amp;= \\frac{100 - 3\\sqrt{x^2 - 900}}{120 - 3x}\\\\ &amp;= \\frac{100 - 3\\sqrt{\\frac{900}{\\sin^2\\theta} - 900}}{120 - \\frac{90}{\\sin\\theta}}\\\\ &amp;= \\frac{100 - 90\\sqrt{\\csc^2\\theta - 1}}{120 - \\frac{90}{\\sin\\theta}}\\\\ &amp;= \\frac{100 - \\frac{90}{\\tan\\theta}}{120 - \\frac{90}{\\sin\\theta}}\\\\ &amp;= \\frac{100\\sin\\theta - 90\\cos\\theta}{120\\sin\\theta - 90}\\\\ &amp;= \\frac{10\\sin\\theta - 9\\cos\\theta}{12\\sin\\theta - 9}\\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"224\" height=\"304\" />\n</p><p>Now we have: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/d/3cd7c497a24b4b8dcc255bd51eb3adc33a0b60be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos\\theta = \\frac{10\\sin\\theta - 9\\cos\\theta}{12\\sin\\theta - 9},\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"37\" /> meaning that: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/d/21da66bcb16871895b31d0df90730ae653e1d233.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[12\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta - 9\\cos\\theta = 10\\sin\\theta - 9\\cos\\theta \\implies \\cos\\theta = \\frac{10}{12} = \\frac56.\\]\" width=\"488\" height=\"38\" />\nThis means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/516110715d10f1e50f03a84e71243b1b4706290f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\arccos\\left(\\frac56\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"126\" height=\"45\" />, giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfc308ff37f94838c11808d9746f10ba1ac15deb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{A}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~ap246\n</p><p>why would you EVER do this to yourself 😭😭\n</p><p>- PerseverePlayer\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28No_Trig.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(No_Trig)\">Solution 4 (No Trig)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (No Trig)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/3/783d500281f8f46167dff3b071c543d42150e67f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DP$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />. Apply the Pythagoras theorem on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f4326fc15c7fb36578bfb20151906ed280a87526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ADP}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741ad66dface14f5a69b3905458260df424da4ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = \\sqrt{900 + x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"136\" height=\"21\" />, which is also the length of every zigzag segment. \n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/c/05cf902981f5aa2c2e40947046ad9df9e4673195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{100}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" /> such segments. Thus the total length formed by the zigzags is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f366c80ca579b3805319fcb33ea29e585f13643b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{100}{x} \\times \\sqrt{900+x^2} = 120\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/e/16ea7a69174caa59506c95ed4ed280b8d98500e0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{900+x^2} = \\frac{6}{5}x\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/6/1e6611586517cd1a99ec35d16f31f5d0bbdd16b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[900 + x^2 = \\frac{36}{25}x^2\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/8/d9853c58c2bda5d4f711022e995240636f92a094.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac{150}{\\sqrt{11}} = DP\\]\" width=\"125\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/a/b6aa16db0f1b1e073bd20856be1f5d03bad85488.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AP = \\sqrt{900 + x^2} = \\frac{180}{\\sqrt{11}}\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/5/d552813386b6dd3af0e8380a9d1e122bf689c4d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos\\theta = \\frac{DP}{AP} = \\frac{5}{6}\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/4/8a4b1e88d5038c815094e93d73af7347228ab23e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\theta=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } \\arccos\\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)}\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"54\" />\n</p><p>(note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/c/05cf902981f5aa2c2e40947046ad9df9e4673195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{100}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" /> is not an integer, but it doesn't matter because of similar triangles. The length of the incomplete segment is always proportionate to the length of the incomplete base)\n</p><p>~dwarf_marshmallow\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Intuitive_and_Quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Intuitive_and_Quick)\">Solution 5 (Intuitive and Quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Intuitive and Quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Imagine that Usain walks at a constant speed. The horizontal component of Usain's velocity does not change. (Imagine a beam of light reflecting off of mirrors. A mirror only changes the velocity of light in the direction perpendicular to the mirror.) The horizontal component of Usain's velocity divided by his total velocity must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d4a6987dcff616a5d69e233bf544052449c45da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{100}{120}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/4/8a4b1e88d5038c815094e93d73af7347228ab23e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\theta=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } \\arccos\\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)}\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"54\" />.\n~numerophile\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Although the diagram is not fully accurate, we can use it to some extent. \n</p><p>It's given that the length of the rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and the total length of the path Usain is taking is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, so Usain will walk <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/4/554a223e1705473faf69a9c0dd629ada8f62c652.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{120}{100} = \\frac{6}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"38\" /> longer than he would if he were just to walk along the rectangle. Therefore for each point along his path, he will travel <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4fc4c669518d5da6185c95ea46645895843844d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> farther than he would if he were just to walk along the rectangle. \n</p><p>Drop a perpendicular from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/e/3eea6d4459f92704a985331333ad06bbc262323c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />: it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/1/4a1b6e8bd6208f4450a519cc9e83a640b5279c79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QP = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/c/7ec79b680b361fa5e4da1d0b12f3c9bfe5d6bfa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA = \\frac{6}{5}x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" /> By the Pythagorean Theorem, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e2089d27a859e6e2f6106eb55b3524e1f7e798f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 + 900 = \\frac{36}{25}x,\\]\" width=\"127\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/d/ebdf769fe279d51c981015a7b20bb1193040e7d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{150}{\\sqrt{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"74\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec392a19a1e61c840e75adb88220b7993b9679c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6x}{5} = \\frac{180}{\\sqrt{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"87\" height=\"43\" />. \n</p><p>Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6fa720d96ac2c556ed15dce98f05b1fb1ff98c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta = \\frac{\\frac{150}{\\sqrt{11}}}{\\frac{180}{\\sqrt{11}}} = \\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"132\" height=\"54\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/7/9c70286e77b81336db9a901e267054655426e3cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } \\arccos\\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"181\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p><br />\n-Benedict T (countmath1)\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Very_Bashy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Very_Bashy)\">Solution 7 (Very Bashy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Very Bashy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we test that we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> segments. If there were only two segments, then the length of each one would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/8/b483bbda40bfbb6a31d6289372a4b0a23138b979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{50^2+30^2} = 10\\sqrt{34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"166\" height=\"21\" />. Then the length of two segments would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/c/95c9923011ee7d1d3dfbbbcfa0bdfcf7cc4a6de9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\sqrt{34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"21\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/5/2155636fbf7ce822d2c963f16f2ee6f2f1681112.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> is a bit less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, it is safe to say we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> segments. The length of the first two segments would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/a/49a0fa66b40fd3fb57537c5573ed991de0faf5c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{30*2}{\\sin{\\theta}} = \\frac{60}{\\sin{\\theta}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"113\" height=\"38\" />. The width  remaining for the third segment would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/e/e5ec204f9fad2754198c28141356afeabeb08518.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 - \\frac{30*2}{\\tan{\\theta}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"38\" /> and thus the length of the third segment would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/a/5ea831e95b4b31e8648a1699724b0a7053f65683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{100 - \\frac{30*2}{\\tan{\\theta}}}{\\cos{\\theta}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"42\" />. Now, we have a very bashy equation that we have to solve.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/9/4b970f5fa1c3ed3bf40f693fbbf07e60fce996be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{60}{\\sin{\\theta}} + \\frac{100 - \\frac{60}{\\tan{\\theta}}}{\\cos{\\theta}} = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"200\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb82cfd63825c2e508cb26b55435954828ef7ade.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{\\sin{\\theta}} + \\frac{5 - \\frac{3}{\\tan{\\theta}}}{\\cos{\\theta}} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"163\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d80ade6ae64cd07f55eb274beba23f8a2cddd51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{\\sin{\\theta}} + \\frac{5 - \\frac{3}{\\frac{\\sin{\\theta}}{\\cos{\\theta}}}}{\\cos{\\theta}} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"162\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/6/f466f92419027620ac38ae182391a33b96b84854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{\\sin{\\theta}} + \\frac{5 - \\frac{3\\cdot\\cos{\\theta}}{\\sin{\\theta}}}{\\cos{\\theta}} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"172\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/255ecf4099bdb4717206ffe1ba11fc15d5cd3ee2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{\\sin{\\theta}} + \\frac{5}{\\cos{\\theta}} - \\frac{3}{\\sin{\\theta}} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"197\" height=\"38\" /> (oh look, it cancels out)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/6707b04f25b19f9386581d08eccf708cbed9ea46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{\\cos{\\theta}} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/40553bc78dbb8b9a10bef2366578d6c5826ba2d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{\\theta} = \\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/0/a2073f4856f729530df4e26f770eef46bd6b99d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\arccos{\\frac{5}{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f20f148f47b814b04d70e693c162fde1308629eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } \\arccos\\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"143\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p>~ROGER8432V3\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28easy_to_digest.29_by_Power_Solve\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(easy_to_digest)_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution (easy to digest) by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (easy to digest) by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YXIH3UbLqK8?si=U1VEKC7S0PoUFjF5&amp;t=2100\">https://youtu.be/YXIH3UbLqK8?si=U1VEKC7S0PoUFjF5&amp;t=2100</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/NhUI-BNCIUE\">https://youtu.be/NhUI-BNCIUE</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28.E2.9A.A1Solved_in_56_seconds.E2.9A.A1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(⚡Solved_in_56_seconds⚡)\">Video Solution (⚡Solved in 56 seconds⚡)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (⚡Solved in 56 seconds⚡)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jkujDM5aW3w\">https://youtu.be/jkujDM5aW3w</a> \n<i> ~Education, the Study of Everything</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ianRnPT_jk4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ianRnPT_jk4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/S5H8JEImiA8\">https://youtu.be/S5H8JEImiA8</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A\">2023 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem